{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2788533bf745abc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Component: ogx-k8s-operator\n2\t\n3\t## Metadata\n4\t\n5\t- **Repository**: https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/ogx-k8s-operator.git\n6\t- **Version**: 53675d4fc305426fd9ae2d04626509a1af11f5d7\n7\t- **Distribution**: RHOAI\n8\t- **Languages**: Go\n9\t- **Deployment Type**: Kubernetes Operator / Controller\n10\t- **Generated By**: Claude Opus 4.6 on 2026-08-13\n11\t\n12\t## Purpose\n13\t\n14\t**Short**: Kubernetes operator that manages OGX inference servers on RHOAI, reconciling OGXServer custom resources into fully configured deployments with autoscaling, network policies, monitoring, and a validating admission webhook. [source: main.go:101, api/v1beta1/ogxserver_webhook.go:54, config/rbac/role.yaml:2]\n15\t\n16\t**Detailed**: ogx-k8s-operator ships two controller-runtime binaries. The root `ogx-k8s-operator` binary runs the OGXServerReconciler, which watches OGXServer CRs (ogx.io/v1beta1) and reconciles each into a Deployment, Service, HPA, PDB, NetworkPolicy, ConfigMap, and optional Ingress and PersistentVolumeClaim. It label-filters its informer caches to only track resources with `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: ogx-operator` and applies the cluster's OpenShift TLS profile (with an Intermediate fallback on non-OpenShift clusters) to the webhook server. The `ogx-module` binary is a separate controller-runtime operator that manages the OGX platform component CRD (components.platform.opendatahub.io/OGX) and uses odh-platform-utilities for kustomize-based manifest rendering, condition management, garbage collection, and platform detection. A `configgen` CLI generates runtime configuration from distribution specifications. A validating webhook (`vogxserver.kb.io`) enforces OGXServer schema integrity on CREATE and UPDATE operations with a Fail failure policy. [source: main.go:101-106, main.go:108-136, main.go:156-198, ogx-module/internal/controller/ogx/reconciler.go:15-20, config/webhook/manifests.yaml:2-27, Dockerfile.konflux:29]\n17\t\n18\t## Architectural Analysis\n19\t\n20\togx-k8s-operator follows a dual-binary operator pattern common in the RHOAI platform. The root operator (`ogx-k8s-operator`) owns the user-facing OGXServer CR lifecycle, while `ogx-module` manages the platform-level OGX component CRD that the RHOAI operator uses to install and configure OGX itself. This separation keeps the user-facing reconciliation loop independent of the platform bootstrapping logic.\n21\t\n22\tThe OGXServerReconciler owns a broad set of child resources—Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, HPAs, PDBs, NetworkPolicies, Ingresses, PVCs, and Secrets—and uses label-scoped informer caches (`app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: ogx-operator`) to reduce watch pressure on the API server. It also watches Secrets and ConfigMaps with a dedicated label selector rather than listing the entire namespace, which is a meaningful isolation boundary in multi-tenant clusters. A legacy adoption path exists for migrating pre-existing resources under operator management (controllers/legacy_adoption.go).\n23\t\n24\tTLS configuration is delegated to the OpenShift platform: the operator fetches the APIServer TLS profile at startup via `controller-runtime-common/pkg/tls.FetchAPIServerTLSProfile` and applies it to the webhook server, falling back to the Intermediate profile on non-OpenShift clusters or transient API errors. This means cipher suite and minimum TLS version are platform-managed rather than hardcoded.\n25\t\n26\tThe ogx-module controller relies heavily on odh-platform-utilities for kustomize-based manifest rendering, controller condition helpers, garbage collection, and platform detection (ODH vs RHOAI). It manages ValidatingWebhookConfigurations, CRDs, RBAC resources, and Deployments as owned resources, providing full lifecycle management for the root operator's installation. Prometheus monitoring integration is established via RBAC grants on monitoring.coreos.com PrometheusRules and ServiceMonitors. [source: main.go:108-136, main.go:156-198, ogx-module/internal/controller/ogx/reconciler.go:15-20, config/rbac/role.yaml:2]\n27\t\n28\t## Provenance\n29\t\n30\t### Repo Lineage\n31\t\n32\t| Role | Repository | Sync Mechanism | Sync Branch | Sync Workflows | Detection Method |\n33\t|----|----------|--------------|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n34\t| Upstream | https://github.com/opendatahub-io/ogx-k8s-operator | auto_merge | odh | -- | sync_config |\n35\t| Downstream | https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/ogx-k8s-operator | auto_merge | odh | -- | local_analysis |\n36\t\n37\t### Aliases\n38\t\n39\t| Current Name | Previous Name | Type | Context |\n40\t|------------|-------------|----|-------|\n41\t\n42\t## Architecture Components\n43\t\n44\t| Component | Type | Purpose |\n45\t|---------|----|-------|\n46\t| Dockerfile.konflux:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n47\t| Dockerfile:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n48\t| OGX controller | Controller | Reconciles OGX resources |\n49\t| OGXServer controller | Controller | Reconciles OGXServer resources |\n50\t| configgen | Go executable | cmd/configgen |\n51\t| ogx-k8s-operator | Go controller-runtime operator | Go entrypoint |\n52\t| ogx-k8s-operator-controller-manager | Deployment | manager (controller:latest) |\n53\t| ogx-module | Go controller-runtime operator | cmd/ogx-module |\n54\t| ogx-module/Dockerfile.konflux:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n55\t| ogx-module/Dockerfile:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n56\t\n57\t## APIs Exposed\n58\t\n59\t### Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)\n60\t\n61\tCRD count scope: 3 core API CRDs; 3 total CRD/API rows including configuration and visibility APIs.\n62\t\n63\t| Group | Version | Kind | Scope | API Role | Purpose |\n64\t|-----|-------|----|-----|--------|-------|\n65\t| components.platform.opendatahub.