onfiguration import | dependency-signal |\n274\t\n275\t### FIPS Compliance\n276\t\n277\tBoth Konflux Dockerfiles build with `CGO_ENABLED=1` (dynamic linking), which satisfies the check-payload requirement for dynamically linked Go binaries. The runtime base image is `registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9/ubi-minimal`, which includes OpenSSL. However, neither Dockerfile specifies `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` or `-tags strictfipsruntime` in the build command, so the Go binaries do not use the strict FIPS runtime enforcement available in Go 1.24+.\n278\t\n279\tAt the application level, the root operator delegates TLS configuration to the OpenShift platform by fetching the APIServer TLS profile via `controller-runtime-common/pkg/tls.FetchAPIServerTLSProfile` and applying it to the webhook server. On non-OpenShift clusters, it falls back to the Intermediate TLS profile. This means cipher suites and minimum TLS version are determined by the platform's TLS security policy rather than hardcoded in the operator. The operator imports `crypto/tls` from the standard library, which on RHEL 9 with CGO delegates to OpenSSL at runtime. No non-FIPS crypto libraries or hardcoded cipher suites were detected.\n280\t\n281\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n282\t|--------|-------|--------|\n283\t| **Build flags** | CGO_ENABLED=1; no GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime | Dockerfile.konflux:6, 29; ogx-module/Dockerfile.konflux:5, 21 |\n284\t| **Linking** | Dynamic (CGO) | Dockerfile.konflux:6; ogx-module/Dockerfile.konflux:5 |\n285\t| **OpenSSL in image** | Yes (via UBI9 minimal base) | Dockerfile.konflux:33; ogx-module/Dockerfile.konflux:24 |\n286\t| **TLS configuration** | Platform-delegated via OpenShift APIServer TLS profile; Intermediate fallback | main.go:156-198 |\n287\t| **Crypto libraries** | stdlib crypto/tls (FIPS via OpenSSL on RHEL 9), controller-runtime-common/pkg/tls | main.go:21, 33 |\n288\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | None detected; no GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime means FIPS mode is not strictly enforced at the Go runtime level | Dockerfile.konflux:29; ogx-module/Dockerfile.konflux:21 |\n289\t## Admission Webhooks\n290\t\n291\t| Name | Type | Path | Port | Failure Policy | Resources | Operations | Purpose |\n292\t|----|----|----|----|--------------|---------|----------|-------|\n293\t| vogxserver.kb.io | Validating | /validate-ogx-io-v1beta1-ogxserver |  | Fail | ogxservers | CREATE, UPDATE |  |\n294\t\n295\t## Data Flows\n296\t\n297\t- **OGXServer reconciliation:** A user creates an OGXServer CR in a namespace. The OGXServerReconciler watches for these CRs and reconciles each into a Deployment running the inference server image, along with a Service, optional HPA, PDB, NetworkPolicy, ConfigMap, Ingress, and PVC. The reconciler reads Secrets (labeled with the watch label) for model credentials and ConfigMaps for runtime configuration. All child resources are owned by the OGXServer CR, enabling garbage collection on deletion. [source: main.go:101-106, main.go:108-136, config/rbac/role.yaml:6-30]\n298\t- **OGX platform component lifecycle:** The ogx-module Reconciler watches the OGX CR (components.platform.opendatahub.io) and renders kustomize-based manifests to install or update the root ogx-k8s-operator Deployment, its RBAC resources, CRDs, ValidatingWebhookConfiguration, and Services. It uses odh-platform-utilities for platform detection (ODH vs RHOAI overlay selection) and condition management. [source: ogx-module/internal/controller/ogx/reconciler.go:15-20, ogx-module/internal/controller/ogx/reconciler.go:44-52]\n299\t- **Admission control:** The ValidatingWebhookConfiguration routes CREATE and UPDATE operations on ogxservers to the `/validate-ogx-io-v1beta1-ogxserver` endpoint served by the ogx-k8s-operator webhook server on port 9443 with TLS. The webhook enforces schema validation with a Fail failure policy. [source: config/webhook/manifests.yaml:2-27, config/webhook/service.yaml:1, api/v1beta1/ogxserver_webhook.go:54]\n300\t- **Monitoring integration:** The operator's RBAC grants allow creating and managing PrometheusRules and ServiceMonitors via the monitoring.coreos.com API group, enabling Prometheus-based observability for managed OGX server instances. [source: config/rbac/role.yaml:2]\n301\t- **Egress:** Both binaries communicate with the Kubernetes API server (port 6443, HTTPS with ServiceAccount token authentication) for all resource operations. The root operator additionally fetches the OpenShift APIServer TLS profile at startup. [source: main.go:156-164, ogx-module/cmd/ogx-module/main.go:66]\n302\t\n303\t## Integration Points\n304\t\n305\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Owns); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: OGXServerReconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]\n306\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Owns); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: Reconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]\n307\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Watches); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: OGXServerReconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]\n308\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Resource CRUD; purpose: create, delete, get, list, patch, update operations by OGXServerReconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]\n309\t- **Additional relationships:** 42 more integration point(s) are listed in the structured table. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, controllers/configmap_reconciler.go:134, 283, 292, controllers/legacy_adoption.go:168, 278, 311, 361]\n310\t\n311\t| Component | Interaction Type | Role | Port | Protocol | Encryption | Purpose |\n312\t|---------|----------------