---|------|------|-----------|\n269\t| tls-config | crypto/tls | TLS configuration import | dependency-signal |\n270\t\n271\t### FIPS Compliance\n272\t\n273\t#### Build-Time FIPS (check-payload gate)\n274\t\n275\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n276\t|--------|-------|--------|\n277\t| **Build flags** | `CGO_ENABLED=1 GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime -tags strictfipsruntime` | Dockerfile.konflux:22 |\n278\t| **Linking** | Dynamic (CGO) | Dockerfile.konflux:22 |\n279\t| **OpenSSL in image** | Yes (via UBI9 minimal base) | Dockerfile.konflux:24 |\n280\t| **OLM FIPS annotation** | not extracted | N/A |\n281\t\n282\t#### Application-Level Crypto\n283\t\n284\t| Aspect | Value | Source |\n285\t|--------|-------|--------|\n286\t| **TLS configuration** | Reads OpenShift cluster TLS security profile via `controller-runtime-common`; applies profile ciphers and min version to webhook/metrics servers | internal/setup/setup.go:103-129 |\n287\t| **Crypto libraries** | stdlib crypto/tls (FIPS via OpenSSL through strictfipsruntime) | internal/setup/setup.go:94, go.mod |\n288\t| **Certificate handling** | TLS certificates for kube-rbac-proxy mounted from Secrets; system trust store for API server | internal/controller/config/templates/deployment.yaml.tmpl:229-230 |\n289\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | None detected; TLS profile inherited from cluster-wide OpenShift configuration | internal/setup/setup.go:115-127 |\n290\t## Admission Webhooks\n291\t\n292\t| Name | Type | Path | Port | Failure Policy | Resources | Operations | Purpose |\n293\t|----|----|----|----|--------------|---------|----------|-------|\n294\t| modelregistries.modelregistry.opendatahub.io | conversion | /convert |  |  | modelregistries | CONVERT |  |\n295\t| mmodelregistry.opendatahub.io | mutating | /mutate-modelregistry-opendatahub-io-modelregistry |  | fail | modelregistries | CREATE, UPDATE |  |\n296\t| vmodelregistry.opendatahub.io | validating | /validate-modelregistry-opendatahub-io-modelregistry |  | fail | modelregistries | CREATE, UPDATE |  |\n297\t\n298\t## Data Flows\n299\t\n300\t- **API request path:** External clients access model-registry instances through Gateway API HTTPRoutes or OpenShift Routes. HTTPRoutes match path prefix `/model-registry/{registry-name}/` and rewrite URLs before forwarding to the backend Service, which targets either the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar (port 8443, TLS-terminated with SubjectAccessReview authorization) or the rest-container directly (port 8080). The kube-rbac-proxy proxies authorized requests to `http://127.0.0.1:{rest-port}/` on the loopback interface. [source: internal/controller/config/templates/gateway/gateway-httproute.yaml.tmpl:22-38, internal/controller/config/templates/deployment.yaml.tmpl:222-224]\n301\t- **Operator control plane:** The operator watches ModelRegistry and Catalog CRs and reconciles the full resource graph — Deployments, Services, ServiceAccounts, Secrets, ConfigMaps, RBAC bindings, NetworkPolicies, and ingress resources. It communicates exclusively with the Kubernetes API server over HTTPS/WSS using its ServiceAccount token, secured by the `model-registry-operator-manager-role` ClusterRole. [source: internal/controller/modelregistry_controller.go:282-304, internal/controller/modelcatalog_controller.go:1353-1361]\n302\t- **Data storage:** Each model-registry instance connects to a PostgreSQL or MySQL database with configurable connection parameters including SSL/TLS certificates, keys, and root CA bundles mounted from Secrets and ConfigMaps. Database credentials are injected via environment variables from referenced Secrets. [source: internal/controller/config/templates/deployment.yaml.tmpl:40-68, 107-131]\n303\t- **Webhook admission:** The operator serves three webhook endpoints — conversion (`/convert`), mutating, and validating — for ModelRegistry resources, enforced via Kubernetes admission webhook configurations with `fail` failure policy. [source: config/webhook/manifests.yaml:2-31, internal/webhook/modelregistry_webhook.go:57-110]\n304\t\n305\t## Integration Points\n306\t\n307\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Watches); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: ModelCatalogReconciler. [source: api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_types.go:157, 440, api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_webhook.go:236, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_types.go:167, 257, 291, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_webhook.go:246]\n308\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Resource CRUD; purpose: delete, get, list, update operations by ModelCatalogReconciler, ModelRegistryReconciler. [source: api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_types.go:157, 440, api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_webhook.go:236, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_types.go:167, 257, 291, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_webhook.go:246]\n309\t- **/v1/Endpoints:** Resource read; purpose: get operations by ModelRegistryReconciler. [source: api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_types.go:157, 440, api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_webhook.go:236, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_types.go:167, 257, 291, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_webhook.go:246]\n310\t- **/v1/PersistentVolumeClaim:** Resource CRUD; purpose: delete, get operations by ModelCatalogReconciler. [source: api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_types.go:157, 440, api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_webhook.go:236, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_types.go:167, 257, 291, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_webhook.go:246]\n311\t- **Additional relationships:** 40 more integration point(s) are listed in the structured table. [source: api/v1alpha1/modelregistry_webhook.go:236, api/v1beta1/modelregistry_webhook.go:246, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, go.mod]\n312\t\n313\t| Component | Interaction Type | Role | Port | Protocol | Encryption | Purpose |\n314\t|---------|----------------|----|----|--------|----------|-------|\n315\t| /v1/ConfigMap | Controller watch (Watches) |  |  | Kubernetes API | TLS | ModelCatalogReconciler |\n316\t| /v1/ConfigMap | Resource CRUD |  |  |  | Unknown | delete, get, list, update operations by ModelCatalogReconciler, ModelRegistryReconciler |\n317\t| /v1/Endpoints | Resource read |  |  |  | Unknown 