| Port | Protocol | Encryption | Purpose |\n=== ai4rag ===\n# Component: ai4rag\n\n## Metadata\n\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/IBM/ai4rag.git\n- **Version**: ca822e846fcfbdadb130bd74af6336bf448ed432\n- **Distribution**: RHOAI\n- **Languages**: Python\n- **Deployment Type**: Application Service\n- **Generated By**: Claude Opus 4.6 on 2026-08-13\n\n## Purpose\n\n**Short**: ai4rag is a Python library that automates the generation and hyperparameter optimization of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) patterns, designed to run as pipeline components within RHOAI Data Science Pipelines. [source: pyproject.toml:6-7, ai4rag/utils/event_handler/event_handler.py:47-55]\n\n**Detailed**: ai4rag provides an end-to-end RAG optimization toolkit that orchestrates document ingestion from S3-compatible storage, text chunking (via Docling and LangChain strategies), embedding generation, vector store indexing (Milvus, PGVector, or Chroma), retrieval, LLM-based answer generation, and evaluation. It uses a hyperparameter optimization loop based on Generalized Additive Models (GAM) to search over chunking parameters, embedding models, foundation models, and retrieval strategies, producing ranked RAG pattern configurations. The library connects to an OpenAI-compatible Model-as-a-Service (MaaS) endpoint for both LLM inference and embedding generation, and includes a KFP event handler for integration with Data Science Pipelines. It is packaged as a Python library with no HTTP server or Kubernetes deployment manifests of its own. [source: pyproject.toml:6-7, 30-44, ai4rag/components/utils/maas_client.py:30-62, ai4rag/utils/event_handler/event_handler.py:47-55, ai4rag/core/hpo/gam_opt.py:1]\n\n## Architectural Analysis\n\nai4rag is structured as a layered Python library organized around a RAG pipeline lifecycle: data ingestion, chunking, embedding, vector store management, retrieval, LLM generation, and evaluation. The optimization layer wraps this pipeline in a hyperparameter search driven by a GAM-based optimizer that explores combinations of chunking strategies (Docling hierarchical, LangChain recursive), embedding models, foundation models, and retrieval parameters to produce ranked RAG pattern configurations. [source: ai4rag/components/optimization/rag_templates_optimization.py:1-46, ai4rag/core/hpo/gam_opt.py:1]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91a9c2264e52e415","agent_id":"a119942f9f83e0558","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"2df10434-75e4-49e4-bcad-e10d998956eb","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:18:58.522Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c1633047806daef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
