{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0b2bee3e-fb03-4389-9515-2fd4a7429ee4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9968d3bccb7a49a6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-rs8r4br_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes Gen AI Studio playground RAG use OGX's existing remote pgvector\nvector_io provider, backed by a PostgreSQL database, instead of depending on\nthe inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the OGX distribution.\nThe gen-ai BFF creates OGXServer instances for the playground; this epic\nextends that configuration path so playgrounds with RAG get the remote pgvector\nprovider, including a bring-your-own path where the user supplies PostgreSQL\nconnection details. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector\nstore implementation is largely reusable — the work is configuration and\nwiring, not a new provider.\n\n## Scope\n\n- When the gen-ai BFF creates or updates OGXServer instances for playgrounds\n  with RAG enabled, set the remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration\n  (activated via the distribution's pgvector provider environment guard) with\n  PostgreSQL connection details sourced from a secret.\n- Support a user-provided (bring-your-own) PostgreSQL connection string so\n  playground RAG functions with no platform-provisioned database — this is the\n  fallback path if platform self-provisioning is not available in 3.5, and it\n  unblocks validation work independently of the provisioning decision.\n- Leave OGX application storage configuration untouched: vector storage and\n  application storage are independent configurations, and the application\n  storage backend remains on its existing SQLite default. No storage\n  consolidation and no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is introduced.\n- Verify, and capture as configuration guidance, that switching from the\n  default pgvector store to an external vector database is a configuration\n  change of the vector_io provider — this addresses the strategy's open\n  question about a migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A playground with RAG enabled, configured with a user-provided PostgreSQL\n  instance (with pgvector), stores and retrieves vector embeddings through the\n  remote pgvector provider: document upload, embedding, retrieval, and\n  generation complete successfully.\n- The vector store in use runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX\n  instance (a remote provider, not an inline provider bundled in the OGX\n  process).\n- OGX application storage configuration is unchanged from its existing default\n  (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is introduced by this change).\n- Switching the vector_io provider from the default pgvector store to an\n  external vector database is achievable through configuration only, and the\n  required configuration is captured as guidance.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no\n  loss of current capability): this epic delivers the provider path; full\n  no-loss verification is completed by the validation and benchmark work.\n- AC-4 (default vector store runs as a separate process, not an inline\n  provider): delivered by selecting the remote pgvector provider.\n- SE-1 (bring-your-own PostgreSQL support via user-configured connection\n  details).\n- SE-4 (application storage untouched; no storage migration).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The ogx-distribution already ships the remote pgvector provider (inline\n  providers are stripped from the distribution build); no OGX code change is\n  expected. If the provider guard or its configuration surface turns out to\n  require distribution changes, that scope must be re-evaluated against the\n  OGX distribution component.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92226,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91a9c2264e52e415","agent_id":"a119942f9f83e0558","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"066105fa-13ef-4bf8-b081-e8323ed2c832","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:24:04.586Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
