{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d1ae5317-551d-4961-90b0-48d5098580ea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-897a0e1b2cfa89de","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-rs8r4br_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (operator path)\n\n## Description\n\nThis branch epic applies when the provisioning-approach decision selects\noperator-based self-provisioning — i.e. the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\ndelivered by the dashboard operator modularization will be available for\nRHOAI 3.5. It implements PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI\nStudio playgrounds in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's\nauto-provisioned database pattern, so that a default vector store works\nout-of-the-box with no manual setup. The upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot\ncarry this logic; it lives in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer.\n\n## Scope\n\n- In the RHOAI-controlled operator layer provided by the dashboard operator\n  modularization: manage the lifecycle of an auto-provisioned PostgreSQL\n  instance for Gen AI Studio playgrounds (Deployment, Service, credentials\n  secret), following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern.\n- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image, which already includes pgvector\n  — no custom image build and no new build-pipeline onboarding; reuse the\n  existing related-image reference so disconnected installs resolve the image.\n- Scope the provisioned instance per namespace (per the scoping-model decision)\n  for multi-tenant isolation.\n- Ensure the provisioned instance's connection details flow into the\n  playground's OGXServer remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration, so\n  a playground with RAG works out of the box with zero manual steps.\n- Design for portability: the component consumes a connection string rather\n  than owning provisioning indefinitely — when the platform-provided shared\n  PostgreSQL (managed via the DSC) becomes available in RHOAI 3.6, switching to\n  the shared connection string is a configuration change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user creates a playground with RAG enabled and a working default vector\n  store exists with zero manual provisioning or configuration steps.\n- The provisioned PostgreSQL runs as a separate process from the OGX instance,\n  scoped per namespace (multi-tenant isolation), and the playground's vector\n  traffic goes through the remote pgvector provider.\n- Resource requests/limits for the provisioned instance are set from the\n  agreed reference sizing (model-registry-operator values adjusted by the\n  benchmark results).\n- No custom container image is built or onboarded for this capability: the\n  existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector is used via the existing\n  related-image reference.\n- Switching the playground to a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL connection\n  string requires configuration only (portability verified).\n- Playground deletion cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources the\n  operator created for it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n  provisioning of external infrastructure).\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no\n  loss of capability) — completes the out-of-box path on top of the provider\n  configuration capability.\n- AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance).\n- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation).\n- SE-2 (portability to the 3.6 platform-shared PostgreSQL via connection\n  string).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Hard precondition: the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164)\n  must deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator layer; this epic exists only on\n  that outcome. If the operator layer is not ready for 3.5, self-provisioning\n  falls back to the BFF-managed path or to bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n- The upstream ogx-k8s-operator is not modified by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":93995,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91a9c2264e52e415","agent_id":"a119942f9f83e0558","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"a6826113-c257-4995-b051-272acfaf085b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:24:27.192Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
