{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e4a8f37ea53fbb6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004 (Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio and Auto Rag)\n11\t\n12\t## Input Basis and Precedence\n13\t\n14\tThe strategy's full technical detail is stored as a Jira attachment\n15\t(`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) that is **not available in this workspace** — the\n16\tAffected Components, Impacted Teams, High Level Requirements, Dependencies, and\n17\tNon-Functional Requirements tables could not be read. The decomposition is\n18\ttherefore derived from the Jira issue body (Summary, Problem Statement,\n19\tAcceptance Criteria, Success Criteria, Open Questions) and the **Staff Engineer\n20\tInput, which takes precedence** per the parsing rules. Requirements are\n21\tidentified below as AC-1..AC-6 (from the body's Acceptance Criteria) and\n22\tSE-1..SE-4 (Staff Engineer directives). See Health Warnings.\n23\t\n24\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides (traceability)\n25\t\n26\tThe Staff Engineer Input diverges from the AI-generated technical approach\n27\t(which resides in the unavailable attachment). Logged overrides applied to this\n28\tdecomposition:\n29\t\n30\t1. **OGX does not auto-provision PostgreSQL.** OGX defaults to SQLite for\n31\t   application storage; the odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF hardcodes SQLite when\n32\t   creating OGXServer instances. Introducing PostgreSQL for pgvector is new\n33\t   work, not an extension of existing infrastructure. No epic assumes an\n34\t   existing per-instance PostgreSQL database.\n35\t2. **No custom image build and no Konflux onboarding.** The Red Hat\n36\t   `postgresql-16` image already includes pgvector, the model-registry-operator\n37\t   already auto-provisions it, and a related-image reference already exists for\n38\t   disconnected installs. The onboarding chain (image build, Konflux, license\n39\t   scanning epics) is eliminated entirely.\n40\t3. **Decoupled from Auto Rag.** Auto Rag compatibility is RHAISTRAT-7824 scope\n41\t   (RHOAI 3.6). Auto Rag is removed from affected components, acceptance\n42\t   criteria, and validation scope. AC-3 is therefore not covered by any epic\n43\t   (see Health Warnings).\n44\t4. **Performance scope is dev-experimentation.** No latency SLAs; the benchmark\n45\t   verifies pgvector is the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus\n46\t   baseline; flat scan (no index) is sufficient for typical playground document\n47\t   sets. The strategy's latency/corpus-size/index-type open questions are\n48\t   removed.\n49\t5. **Vector storage and application storage are independent.** Only the\n50\t   `vector_io` pgvector provider is configured; application storage stays on\n51\t   SQLite. No storage-consolidation or SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration work.\n52\t6. **3.5 must self-provision; 3.6 moves to a platform-shared PostgreSQL.** Any\n53\t   provisioning implemented now must be portable to consuming a shared\n54\t   connection string later.\n55\t7. **Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164** (dashboard operator modularization,\n56\t   In Progress) for operator-based self-provisioning, with defined fallbacks\n57\t   (bring-your-own PostgreSQL, or BFF-managed provisioning). Modeled as the\n58\t   gating Investigation with conditional branches and a tiered delivery.\n59\t\n60\t## Component Mapping Notes\n61\t\n62\t- All epics use the canonical component **Gen AI Studio**: the work lives in\n63\t  the odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF and the RHOAI-controlled operator layer that the\n64\t  dashboard operator modularization will provide.\n65\t- **ogx-distribution (OGX) is a passive component**: its remote pgvector\n66\t  `vector_io` provider already exists (corroborated by\n67\t  `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ogx-distribution.md`,\n68\t  which lists PGVector as an existing optional vector backend and notes inline\n69\t  providers are already stripped from the distribution build). No OGX code\n70\t  changes; validation is folded into acceptance criteria on the Gen AI Studio\n71\t  epics. No `LlamaStack`/`OGX Core` epic is generated.\n72\t- **rhods-operator**: no work — the PostgreSQL related-image reference already\n73\t  exists per Staff Engineer Input.\n74\t- **model-registry-operator**: reference pattern only (PostgreSQL\n75\t  auto-provisioning and resource sizing); no changes.\n76\t\n77\t## Epic List\n78\t\n79\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n80\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n81\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Decide the default vector store provisioning approach for Gen AI Studio | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n82\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n83\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Validate and benchmark pgvector as the default vector store for playground RAG | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n84\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 | Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (operator path) | Implementation (branch A) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n85\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning for Gen AI Studio (fallback path) | Implementation (branch B) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n86\t\n87\tMain-plan epics: E001–E003. Branch epics (BRANCH-A-E004, BRANCH-B-E004) are\n88\tconditional alternatives selected by the E001 outcome; they are attached to the\n89\tgating Investigation as plan documents, not standalone main-plan nodes.\n90\t\n91\t## Dependency DAG\n92\t\n93\t```mermaid\n94\tgraph TD\n95\t    E001[\"E001 Provisioning approach go/no-go\"]\n96\t    E002[\"E002 pgvector vector_io provider config\"]\n97\t    E003[\"E003 pgvector validation and benchmark\"]\n98\t    BEA[\"BRANCH-A-E004 Operator-based provisioning\"]\n99\t    BEB[\"BRANCH-B-E004 BFF-managed provisioning\"]\n100\t    E002 --> E003\n101\t    E001 --> BEA\n102\t    E001 --> BEB\n103\t    E002 --> BEB\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\tMain-plan critical path: E002 → E003 (length 2). Branch epics are excluded\n107\tfrom the main-plan critical path; the branch-extended longest path is\n108\tE001 → E002 → BRANCH-B-E004 (length 3).\n109\t\n110\t## DAG Justification\n111\t\n112\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n113\t|------|------|-----------|\n114\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates) | The operator-path epic exists only if the go/no-go decides the dashboard operator modularization will land for 3.5. True gate: `remove` if the operator layer is not available. |\n115\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates) | The BFF-managed fallback epic exists only if the go/no-go selects that fallback. True gate: `remove` if operator-based provisioning is chosen or the fallback is deemed too risky. |\n116\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (consumer) | The validation/benchmark exercises the pgvector provider configuration capability; it builds on and verifies that surface. |\n117\t| E002 → BRANCH-B-E004 | Rule 13 / boundary rule | The BFF-managed provisioning extends the same gen-ai BFF playground/OGXServer-creation surface that carries the provider configuration; a serial edge avoids two epics independently building the same surface. |\n118\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | The decision work and the provider-configuration work are independent (the configuration accepts any PostgreSQL connection string regardless of who provisions it); they run in parallel. |\n119\t| E002 ∥ BRANCH-A-E004 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different codebases (gen-ai BFF vs the new operator layer), no shared build-against artifact; the real coupling — a working out-of-box default — is an acceptance criterion on the branch epic, not a DAG edge. |\n120\t| BRANCH-A-E004 ∥ BRANCH-B-E004 (no edge) | Branch semantics | Mutually exclusive conditional alternatives; never both in the plan. |\n121\t\n122\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n123\t\n124\tRequirements are the body's Acceptance Criteria (AC-n) plus Staff Engineer\n125\tdirectives (SE-n); the strategy's own HLR table was in the unavailable\n126\tattachment. All are treated as P0 given the strategy's Blocker priority.\n127\t\n128\t| Requirement | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n129\t|-------------|----------|---------|-------|\n130\t| AC-1: Default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning | P0 | BRANCH-A-E004 or BRANCH-B-E004 (branch-selected) | Tier 2 — delivered by whichever provisioning path the go/no-go selects. On the BYO-only outcome no epic delivers AC-1 this release (see Tiered Delivery). |\n131\t| AC-2: Playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability | P0 | E002, E003, BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | E002 delivers the provider path (BYO), E003 verifies no-loss-of-capability, branch epic completes the out-of-box default. |\n132\t| AC-3: Auto Rag functions with the default vector store | — | (none) | **Removed by Staff Engineer Input** — Auto Rag is RHAISTRAT-7824 scope (3.6). Logged as override, not an orphaned requirement. |\n133\t| AC-4: Default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Remote pgvector provider (not inline); passive ogx-distribution validation folded into E002/E003 acceptance criteria. |\n134\t| AC-5: Scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation) | P0 | E001 (decision), BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 (implementation) | Scoping model resolved by the investigation; implemented by the selected provisioning epic. |\n135\t| AC-6: Lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments | P0 (**bundled**) | E003, BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Bundled into E003: measured by the same benchmark run that verifies AC-2 — same experiment, same deliverable; splitting would duplicate the benchmark. Resource requests/limits set in the branch epic. |\n136\t| SE-1: Bring-your-own PostgreSQL support (user-configured OGXServer connection details) | P0 | E002 | Fallback path that also enables Tier 1 value. |\n137\t| SE-2: Portability to the 3.6 platform-shared PostgreSQL (consume a connection string) | P0 | BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 | Acceptance criterion on whichever provisioning epic lands. |\n138\t| SE-3: Resource sizing referenced from the model-registry-operator | P0 | E003 | Benchmark output feeds the branch epic's sizing. |\n139\t| SE-4: Application storage untouched (no storage migration) | P0 | E002 | Scope constraint on the provider-configuration epic. |\n140\t\n141\tFull coverage: every in-scope requirement maps to at least one epic; no epic is\n142\torphaned (each traces to at least one requirement).\n143\t\n144\t## Health Warnings\n145\t\n146\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the full strategy attachment\n147\t  (`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) was not available, so the Affected Components,\n148\t  Impacted Teams, HLR, Dependencies, and NFR tables could not be parsed. The\n149\t  decomposition derives requirements from the issue body's Acceptance Criteria\n150\t  and the Staff Engineer Input (which takes precedence). Team attribution\n151\t  defaults to the Gen AI Studio team (dashboard-crimson-scrum per the strategy\n152\t  labels; the Gen AI Studio lead is quoted in the body). If the attachment\n153\t  surfaces additional HLRs, the traceability matrix should be re-checked.\n154\t- **External dependency timing risk:** RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator\n155\t  modularization, In Progress) is a hard precondition for operator-based\n156\t  self-provisioning with uncertain timing. Per Staff Engineer Input the\n157\t  strategy cannot be committed to a release until the go/no-go gate resolves;\n158\t  this is modeled as Investigation E001 with conditional branches rather than\n159\t  a DAG edge to an epic in another strategy.\n160\t- **AC-1 delivery is outcome-dependent:** if the go/no-go selects the BYO-only\n161\t  outcome (neither branch epic lands), the out-of-box default is not delivered\n162\t  in this release and AC-1 is only partially met (works with user-provided\n163\t  PostgreSQL). That is an explicit, staff-acknowledged fallback trade-off, not\n164\t  a coverage gap.\n165\t- **Priority note:** the strategy priority is Blocker, so all derived\n166\t  requirements are P0; the \"lightweight\" requirement (AC-6) is bundled rather\n167\t  than split (see traceability matrix).\n168\t- **Epic size:** all epics stay within the ~2-week epic-size guideline; each is\n169\t  one logical change over a single surface. If the provider-configuration work\n170\t  turns out to require changes across additional BFF packages beyond the\n171\t  playground/OGXServer-creation surface, re-split the epic along those\n172\t  sub-system boundaries.\n173\t- **Minor corroboration gap:** the Staff Engineer's claim that the\n174\t  `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` environment variable already exists in\n175\t  the rhods-operator CSV is not corroborated (nor contradicted) by the\n176\t  provisioned rhods-operator architecture-context file; it was verified by the\n177\t  Staff Engineer against the sclorg PostgreSQL container Dockerfile.\n178\t\n179\t## Tiered Delivery\n180\t\n181\tExternal dependency: RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization),\n182\tuncertain timing. Partial value without it: **yes**.\n183\t\n184\t- **Tier 1 (independent, always delivered):**\n185\t  - E001 — risk-reduction decision (go/no-go gate, scoping model, fallback\n186\t    selection) per the Staff directive to define the gate during sprint\n187\t    planning.\n188\t  - E002 — playground RAG works on pgvector with a user-provided PostgreSQL\n189\t    (BYO path); no functional dependence on inline providers.\n190\t  - E003 — benchmark and functional validation de-risking the pgvector choice\n191\t    and feeding resource sizing.\n192\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated, conditional branches):**\n193\t  - BRANCH-A-E004 — operator-based self-provisioning, gated on the dashboard\n194\t    operator modularization landing for 3.5 (outcome A).\n195\t  - BRANCH-B-E004 — BFF-managed provisioning fallback (outcome B).\n196\t  - Outcome C (BYO-only): no Tier 2 epic; the main plan alone ships, AC-1 is\n197\t    met only via user-provided PostgreSQL, and the out-of-box default is\n198\t    deferred. Captured as each branch epic's gate-failure fallback.\n199\t\n200\tBounded outcomes (3) with conditional decomposition branches, per the\n201\tinvestigation-gating rules.\n202\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80d531b12983c1db","agent_id":"abbd3441d532da3f5","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"a4cd915e-896b-4b22-b312-7c68f46d971d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:27:05.810Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e4a8f37ea53fbb6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
