{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a646a96457ddc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Configure the pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes Gen AI Studio playground RAG use OGX's existing remote pgvector\n34\tvector_io provider, backed by a PostgreSQL database, instead of depending on\n35\tthe inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the OGX distribution.\n36\tThe gen-ai BFF creates OGXServer instances for the playground; this epic\n37\textends that configuration path so playgrounds with RAG get the remote pgvector\n38\tprovider, including a bring-your-own path where the user supplies PostgreSQL\n39\tconnection details. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector\n40\tstore implementation is largely reusable — the work is configuration and\n41\twiring, not a new provider.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- When the gen-ai BFF creates or updates OGXServer instances for playgrounds\n46\t  with RAG enabled, set the remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration\n47\t  (activated via the distribution's pgvector provider environment guard) with\n48\t  PostgreSQL connection details sourced from a secret.\n49\t- Support a user-provided (bring-your-own) PostgreSQL connection string so\n50\t  playground RAG functions with no platform-provisioned database — this is the\n51\t  fallback path if platform self-provisioning is not available in 3.5, and it\n52\t  unblocks validation work independently of the provisioning decision.\n53\t- Leave OGX application storage configuration untouched: vector storage and\n54\t  application storage are independent configurations, and the application\n55\t  storage backend remains on its existing SQLite default. No storage\n56\t  consolidation and no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is introduced.\n57\t- Verify, and capture as configuration guidance, that switching from the\n58\t  default pgvector store to an external vector database is a configuration\n59\t  change of the vector_io provider — this addresses the strategy's open\n60\t  question about a migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- A playground with RAG enabled, configured with a user-provided PostgreSQL\n65\t  instance (with pgvector), stores and retrieves vector embeddings through the\n66\t  remote pgvector provider: document upload, embedding, retrieval, and\n67\t  generation complete successfully.\n68\t- The vector store in use runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX\n69\t  instance (a remote provider, not an inline provider bundled in the OGX\n70\t  process).\n71\t- OGX application storage configuration is unchanged from its existing default\n72\t  (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is introduced by this change).\n73\t- Switching the vector_io provider from the default pgvector store to an\n74\t  external vector database is achievable through configuration only, and the\n75\t  required configuration is captured as guidance.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no\n80\t  loss of current capability): this epic delivers the provider path; full\n81\t  no-loss verification is completed by the validation and benchmark work.\n82\t- AC-4 (default vector store runs as a separate process, not an inline\n83\t  provider): delivered by selecting the remote pgvector provider.\n84\t- SE-1 (bring-your-own PostgreSQL support via user-configured connection\n85\t  details).\n86\t- SE-4 (application storage untouched; no storage migration).\n87\t\n88\t## Risks / Notes\n89\t\n90\t- The ogx-distribution already ships the remote pgvector provider (inline\n91\t  providers are stripped from the distribution build); no OGX code change is\n92\t  expected. If the provider guard or its configuration surface turns out to\n93\t  require distribution changes, that scope must be re-evaluated against the\n94\t  OGX distribution component.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80d531b12983c1db","agent_id":"abbd3441d532da3f5","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"255aedd1-fe1a-4ecd-9b14-684d6049d5d6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:27:09.530Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a646a96457ddc6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
