{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fa07954442eb49b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (operator path)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization does not deliver the\n16\t    RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for 3.5, this epic is removed; self-provisioning\n17\t    falls back to the BFF-managed path or to bring-your-own PostgreSQL (main-plan\n18\t    provider configuration with user-supplied connection details).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 1\n27\t  repo_access: 0\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (operator path)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis branch epic applies when the provisioning-approach decision selects\n40\toperator-based self-provisioning — i.e. the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\n41\tdelivered by the dashboard operator modularization will be available for\n42\tRHOAI 3.5. It implements PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI\n43\tStudio playgrounds in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's\n44\tauto-provisioned database pattern, so that a default vector store works\n45\tout-of-the-box with no manual setup. The upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot\n46\tcarry this logic; it lives in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- In the RHOAI-controlled operator layer provided by the dashboard operator\n51\t  modularization: manage the lifecycle of an auto-provisioned PostgreSQL\n52\t  instance for Gen AI Studio playgrounds (Deployment, Service, credentials\n53\t  secret), following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern.\n54\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image, which already includes pgvector\n55\t  — no custom image build and no new build-pipeline onboarding; reuse the\n56\t  existing related-image reference so disconnected installs resolve the image.\n57\t- Scope the provisioned instance per namespace (per the scoping-model decision)\n58\t  for multi-tenant isolation.\n59\t- Ensure the provisioned instance's connection details flow into the\n60\t  playground's OGXServer remote pgvector vector_io provider configuration, so\n61\t  a playground with RAG works out of the box with zero manual steps.\n62\t- Design for portability: the component consumes a connection string rather\n63\t  than owning provisioning indefinitely — when the platform-provided shared\n64\t  PostgreSQL (managed via the DSC) becomes available in RHOAI 3.6, switching to\n65\t  the shared connection string is a configuration change.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- A user creates a playground with RAG enabled and a working default vector\n70\t  store exists with zero manual provisioning or configuration steps.\n71\t- The provisioned PostgreSQL runs as a separate process from the OGX instance,\n72\t  scoped per namespace (multi-tenant isolation), and the playground's vector\n73\t  traffic goes through the remote pgvector provider.\n74\t- Resource requests/limits for the provisioned instance are set from the\n75\t  agreed reference sizing (model-registry-operator values adjusted by the\n76\t  benchmark results).\n77\t- No custom container image is built or onboarded for this capability: the\n78\t  existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector is used via the existing\n79\t  related-image reference.\n80\t- Switching the playground to a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL connection\n81\t  string requires configuration only (portability verified).\n82\t- Playground deletion cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources the\n83\t  operator created for it.\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual\n88\t  provisioning of external infrastructure).\n89\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no\n90\t  loss of capability) — completes the out-of-box path on top of the provider\n91\t  configuration capability.\n92\t- AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance).\n93\t- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation).\n94\t- SE-2 (portability to the 3.6 platform-shared PostgreSQL via connection\n95\t  string).\n96\t\n97\t## Risks / Notes\n98\t\n99\t- Hard precondition: the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164)\n100\t  must deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator layer; this epic exists only on\n101\t  that outcome. If the operator layer is not ready for 3.5, self-provisioning\n102\t  falls back to the BFF-managed path or to bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n103\t- The upstream ogx-k8s-operator is not modified by this epic.\n104\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80d531b12983c1db","agent_id":"abbd3441d532da3f5","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"a9fc0d3c-e430-4ae6-8e88-5e3a1b7e4626","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:27:13.142Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fa07954442eb49b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
