wer-priority feature\nbeing collapsed. Priority inheritance holds: every epic is P0 and the gating\nInvestigation (E001) is P0.\n\n### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\nNo circular dependencies. Every diagram edge (E002→E003, E001→BRANCH-A-E004,\nE001→BRANCH-B-E004, E002→BRANCH-B-E004) has a matching frontmatter `dependencies`\nentry in the target epic, and vice versa; arrows follow the dependency→dependent\nconvention. No frontmatter dependency references a nonexistent epic. Both branch\nfiles set `branch` (A/B, matching filenames) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001`,\nand no main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its dependencies — the branch-gating\ncontract is fully satisfied. The E002→BRANCH-B-E004 edge is justified (extends the\nsame gen-ai BFF surface E002 builds; serializing avoids two epics independently\nbuilding the same surface), and the E002∥BRANCH-A-E004 parallelism is correctly\nkept as an acceptance-criterion gate (the out-of-box default AC) rather than a DAG\nedge — the config-reference coupling is handled the rule-compliant way. E001∥E002\nparallelism is justified (the provider configuration accepts any connection\nstring regardless of who provisions). No konflux-onboarding, license-validation,\nor repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are\nvacuously satisfied (validator confirms). Critical path length 2 (main plan) fits\nthe strategy size heuristic for a focused single-component strategy.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\nAll five epics are scoped to the single canonical component and team (Gen AI\nStudio), matching the staff-directed scope (Auto Rag decoupled; ogx-distribution\npassive; no rhods-operator or model-registry-operator work). No scope duplication:\nE002 delivers provider configuration, E003 delivers validation/benchmark, the\nbranch epics deliver provisioning — distinct deliverables with the shared surface\ncorrectly serialized via the E002→BRANCH-B edge. No work-product type mixing (no\ncontent authoring bundled wi