{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87086f175868dc45","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Completeness\n9\t  description: 'The full strategy attachment (HLR table, Affected Components, Impacted\n10\t    Teams, NFRs, Prerequisites & Process Gates) was unavailable, so the original HLR\n11\t    table and a possible Documentation Support: Yes requirement could not be verified;\n12\t    if the attachment surfaces, re-check the traceability matrix and whether a docs-authoring\n13\t    epic (Rule 11) is required.'\n14\terror: null\n15\t---\n16\t## Review Summary\n17\t\n18\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n19\tRecommendation: accept\n20\t\n21\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py` exited 0 — epic body sections,\n22\tcanonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance,\n23\timplementation-type parallelism, and epic-size overage triggers all pass).\n24\t\n25\tTriage check: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 5 epics — multi-epic output\n26\tis expected; no triage contradiction.\n27\t\n28\tInputs reviewed: strategy `RHAISTRAT-8004.md`, decomposition summary, epics\n29\tE001–E003, branch epics BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004, and all five ai-signals\n30\trationale files.\n31\t\n32\t## Criterion Details\n33\t\n34\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n35\tThe strategy's own HLR table was in the unavailable attachment; the decomposition\n36\tderives requirements from the body's Acceptance Criteria (AC-1..AC-6) plus Staff\n37\tEngineer directives (SE-1..SE-4), all treated as P0 (Blocker priority) — a sound\n38\tsubstitution, disclosed in Health Warnings. The traceability matrix is present and\n39\tcomplete: every in-scope requirement maps to at least one epic, and no epic is\n40\torphaned. AC-3 (Auto Rag) is not covered by any epic, but this is an explicit,\n41\tstaff-directed removal (Auto Rag is RHAISTRAT-7824 / RHOAI 3.6 scope), logged as\n42\tan override with justification rather than silently dropped. AC-1's coverage is\n43\tbranch-conditional, with the BYO-only outcome disclosed as a staff-acknowledged\n44\ttrade-off in Health Warnings. AC-6 is bundled into E003 with a valid rationale\n45\t(same benchmark run and sizing analysis; splitting would duplicate the experiment)\n46\t— and since all requirements are P0, there is no deferrable lower-priority feature\n47\tbeing collapsed. Priority inheritance holds: every epic is P0 and the gating\n48\tInvestigation (E001) is P0.\n49\t\n50\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n51\tNo circular dependencies. Every diagram edge (E002→E003, E001→BRANCH-A-E004,\n52\tE001→BRANCH-B-E004, E002→BRANCH-B-E004) has a matching frontmatter `dependencies`\n53\tentry in the target epic, and vice versa; arrows follow the dependency→dependent\n54\tconvention. No frontmatter dependency references a nonexistent epic. Both branch\n55\tfiles set `branch` (A/B, matching filenames) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001`,\n56\tand no main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its dependencies — the branch-gating\n57\tcontract is fully satisfied. The E002→BRANCH-B-E004 edge is justified (extends the\n58\tsame gen-ai BFF surface E002 builds; serializing avoids two epics independently\n59\tbuilding the same surface), and the E002∥BRANCH-A-E004 parallelism is correctly\n60\tkept as an acceptance-criterion gate (the out-of-box default AC) rather than a DAG\n61\tedge — the config-reference coupling is handled the rule-compliant way. E001∥E002\n62\tparallelism is justified (the provider configuration accepts any connection\n63\tstring regardless of who provisions). No konflux-onboarding, license-validation,\n64\tor repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are\n65\tvacuously satisfied (validator confirms). Critical path length 2 (main plan) fits\n66\tthe strategy size heuristic for a focused single-component strategy.\n67\t\n68\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n69\tAll five epics are scoped to the single canonical component and team (Gen AI\n70\tStudio), matching the staff-directed scope (Auto Rag decoupled; ogx-distribution\n71\tpassive; no rhods-operator or model-registry-operator work). No scope duplication:\n72\tE002 delivers provider configuration, E003 delivers validation/benchmark, the\n73\tbranch epics deliver provisioning — distinct deliverables with the shared surface\n74\tcorrectly serialized via the E002→BRANCH-B edge. No work-product type mixing (no\n75\tcontent authoring bundled with code). All epics are within the ~2-week guideline,\n76\tand the summary records a concrete re-split trigger for the provider-configuration\n77\tepic (re-split along BFF sub-system boundaries if scope grows beyond the\n78\tplayground/OGXServer-creation surface) — a managed trade-off, not an unactionable\n79\tflag.\n80\t\n81\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n82\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its go/no-go outcome determines which branch epic\n83\texists (operator path, BFF path, or neither), and both branch epics depend on it\n84\twith `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001` — the gate changes downstream structure, not\n85\tjust scheduling. Both branch epics populate `gate_failure_impact` with both\n86\t`action: remove` and a substantive `fallback_approach`. Every `gated_by` target\n87\tappears in the epic's direct `dependencies` list. E002, E003, and the branch epics\n88\tare Implementations producing concrete artifacts (provider configuration, baseline\n89\tand benchmark reports with sizing, provisioned PostgreSQL lifecycle). E003's\n90\tdependency on E002 is an Implementation→Implementation edge, so no `gated_by` is\n91\trequired. No misclassifications.\n92\t\n93\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n94\tType-appropriate signal sets are used throughout: E001 carries\n95\t`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric); all four Implementation epics carry\n96\t`ai_signals` (9-signal rubric); no cross-assignment. Signal values are consistent\n97\twith the rationales and the strategy content: E001's `human_judgment_required: -2`\n98\tis justified (the go/no-go hinges on another team's delivery timing and is\n99\texplicitly assigned to sprint planning) and `source_accessibility: 0` is right\n100\t(the gating answer does not yet exist in any readable artifact). BRANCH-A's\n101\tnegative `open_questions`/`external_dependency` and neutral `repo_access` /\n102\t`existing_foundation` correctly reflect the not-yet-existing operator layer, while\n103\tBRANCH-B's positives match the existing BFF surface with the flagged lifecycle\n104\tdesign risk scored `open_questions: -1`. Calibration of `architecture_claims`\n105\tverified against `.context`: the cited files exist and support the claims —\n106\t`ogx-distribution.md` lists PGVector as an existing optional vector backend,\n107\t`odh-dashboard.md` documents the gen-ai BFF sidecar managing K8s resources, and\n108\t`model-registry-operator.md` documents the auto-provisioned PostgreSQL pattern.\n109\tNo arithmetic or threshold checks performed (computed by the pipeline, per\n110\tinstructions).\n111\t\n112\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n113\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the strategy. No\n114\trule-mandated AC is missing: there are no konflux-chain or docs-authoring epics,\n115\tand E002 — the closest thing to a replacement epic — carries the escape-hatch AC\n116\tthat switching the vector_io provider to an external vector database is\n117\tconfiguration-only, alongside the BYO path. No soft ACs: every AC states a\n118\tcondition on the epic's own deliverable; external risks (RHAISTRAT-7164 timing,\n119\tbenchmark-outcome contingency) are correctly placed in Risks/Notes and Health\n120\tWarnings rather than as ACs. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID —\n121\tthe only cross-epic references are full `RHAISTRAT-8004-*` identifiers and\n122\tfrontmatter dependency entries.\n123\t\n124\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n125\tAll in-scope strategy scope is covered: AC-1/2/4/5/6 and SE-1..SE-4 each map to\n126\tat least one epic; both strategy Open Questions are resolved into epic scope\n127\t(scoping model → E001; migration path → E002's configuration-guidance AC); every\n128\tStaff Engineer correction and directive is traceable (no existing-PG assumption,\n129\tno image build/Konflux, Auto Rag decoupling, dev-experimentation benchmark scope,\n130\tmodel-registry reference sizing, BFF fallback with lifecycle design, reusable\n131\tremote vector store, storage independence). The conditional branches cover all\n132\tthree bounded outcomes — A (operator), B (BFF-managed), and C (BYO-only, captured\n133\tas each branch epic's gate-failure fallback) — matching the tiered delivery.\n134\tStrategy-level risks and the external dependency are carried forward, not\n135\tdropped. One residual, disclosed limitation: the full strategy attachment (HLR\n136\ttable, Affected Components, Impacted Teams, NFRs, Prerequisites & Process Gates)\n137\twas unavailable, so the original HLR table and a possible `Documentation Support:\n138\tYes` requirement could not be verified directly; the decomposition flags this in\n139\tHealth Warnings with the right follow-up (re-check traceability if the attachment\n140\tsurfaces). This is a watch item, not a gap the decomposer could close from the\n141\tavailable inputs.\n142\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fc1f982b4d7f890","agent_id":"af816ad53424fbdb4","session_id":"a1b0ecca-9f9b-42d4-80d1-54b9096b8411","uuid":"973c3597-1da6-4041-8145-d1ef6b16ddf0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:33:27.435Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87086f175868dc45","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
